Subject: [PATCH] docs(r48c): clear the Q6_K shader of HQ finding 1; localise a
 pre-existing defect

HQ finding 1 reported MUL_MAT(type_a=q6_K,m=248320,n=1,k=5120) failing only with
GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_XFOLD=0. Twenty runs per arm on the unmodified tree show both arms
failing at the same rate with the same error value (1/20 each, ERR exactly
1.000000000), so the arm asymmetry in the earlier receipts was sampling noise on a
defect whose measured base rate is 7/140, about 5 percent.

The shader cannot be the cause. With XFOLD=0 and the default DIRECT_SCALES=1, both
barrier() calls and every sccache access are unreachable, and the hoisted activation
tile and its per-sub-block sums are dead. The OFF arm is the shipped decode order.

ERR of exactly 1.000000000 decodes as an all-zero Vulkan destination tensor, which
rules out arithmetic. Allocation is identical between a passing and a failing run and
no bounded host split occurs at this shape, so R46b B7c placement is not involved.
The dispatch geometry at this shape is also correct: it is the only row in the sweep
that exceeds maxComputeWorkGroupCount[0] and takes the z-split, and its coverage is
exact with no tail.

The surviving lead is the wait bookkeeping in ggml_vk_synchronize
(ggml-vulkan.cpp:19978-20047), which is outside lane-236's scope. No source file is
changed by this commit; it carries the report section, the probe receipts, and the
prompts and planted-red patch from the lane.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-236 R48c Q6_K, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
