--- /dev/null
+++ b/R48C-Q6K-PLANTED-RED.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+R48c planted RED -- wrong qh shift in mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp.
+
+Apply:  git apply R48C-Q6K-PLANTED-RED.patch
+Revert: git apply -R R48C-Q6K-PLANTED-RED.patch
+
+What it breaks: qh0_u32 carries the low 2 bits of the 6-bit weight's high pair into
+bit position 4-5 of the packed byte. Shifting by 3 instead of 4 lands them at bit 3-4,
+where bit 3 collides with the top bit of the ql low nibble that is OR'd in on the next
+line, and bit 5 is left clear. Scope, stated precisely: every weight of sub-block 0 whose
+qh low pair is NONZERO decodes wrong -- a pair of 00 contributes 0 under either shift, so
+roughly a quarter of sub-block 0's weights are unaffected. That is still every superblock
+of every row, which is far past any NMSE gate.
+
+Expected: the Q6_K MUL_MAT correctness rows added by this lane must FAIL -- all three
+27B shapes (17408x5120, 5120x17408, 248320x5120), every width n = 1..8, both src1 types,
+and in BOTH arms of GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_XFOLD and BOTH arms of GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES,
+because the corrupted line is upstream of every gate. This is a correctness failure, not
+a perf perturbation: if the perf filter still reports a number and the correctness filter
+reports 0 FAIL, the Q6_K coverage added by this lane is NOT reaching the shader.
+
+diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp
+--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp
++++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp
+@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@
+         const uint32_t ql32_u32_hi4 = (ql32_u32 >> 4) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
+
+         const uint32_t qh_u32 = uint32_t(data_a_packed16[ib0 + i].qh[qh_offset / 2]) | (uint32_t(data_a_packed16[ib0 + i].qh[qh_offset / 2 + 1]) << 16);
+-        const uint32_t qh0_u32 = (qh_u32 & 0x03030303) << 4;
++        const uint32_t qh0_u32 = (qh_u32 & 0x03030303) << 3;
+         const uint32_t qh2_u32 = (qh_u32 & 0x0C0C0C0C) << 2;
+         const uint32_t qh4_u32 = (qh_u32 & 0x30303030);
+         const uint32_t qh6_u32 = (qh_u32 & 0xC0C0C0C0) >> 2;
