+STATISTICS CAVEAT - READ BEFORE ACTING ON THE 0/60 ROWS
+  At a 5% base rate, a 0/60 arm has a one-sided p of about 0.05 on its own. Three different
+  knobs each returned 0/60. At least one of those must be sampling noise, so none of them is
+  evidence of a fix. Discriminating a 5% rate would need roughly 500 runs per arm. These rows
+  are recorded for completeness and MUST NOT be read as "knob X fixes it".
+
+  GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX=0 is provably inert here: the ungated stderr receipt
+  "ggml_vulkan: bounded host split admitted:" (ggml-vulkan.cpp:19618) is absent from BOTH the
+  passing and the failing run captured with GGML_VK_MEMORY_LOGGER=1. No host split occurs at
+  this shape, so R46b B7c placement is not involved and that 0/60 is pure noise. This is the
+  direct proof that the 0/60 rows cannot be trusted.
+
+FAILURE SIGNATURE
+  ERR is exactly 1.000000000 on every failure observed (6 failures across all arms).
+  test-backend-ops nmse = sum((a-b)^2) / sum(a^2) with a = the CPU reference. That equals
+  exactly 1 if and only if b, the Vulkan result, is identically zero. So the failing runs
+  produce an all-zero destination tensor, not a numerically wrong one.
+
+ALLOCATION IS IDENTICAL BETWEEN PASS AND FAIL
+  GGML_VK_MEMORY_LOGGER=1 captured one passing and one failing run. Diff after masking
+  addresses shows ONLY the OK/FAIL lines. No placement, heap, or buffer difference.
+
+DISPATCH GEOMETRY AT THIS SHAPE (checked, correct)
+  ne01 = 248320 > maxComputeWorkGroupCount[0] = 65535, so ggml-vulkan.cpp:12115-12118 takes the
+  z-split: groups_z = 64, groups_x = CEIL_DIV(248320,64) = 3880. ggml_vk_dispatch_pipeline then
+  divides by wg_denoms[0] = rm_kq = 2, giving 1940 x 1 x 64 = 124160 workgroups.
+  Shader main(): first_row = 2*(gl_WorkGroupID.x + 1940*gl_WorkGroupID.z), max 248318, +2 rows
+  = 248320 exactly. No tail, no overlap, no gap. This is the only shape in the whole MUL_MAT
+  sweep that takes the z-split path, and the only ~1 GiB src0 (248320 * 20 * 210 B = 0.97 GiB).
+
+READBACK PATH (inspected, not statistically tested)
+  tests/test-backend-ops.cpp:1555 uses ggml_backend_compare_graph_backend, which computes with
+  the SYNCHRONOUS ggml_backend_graph_compute (ggml-backend.cpp:2827-2828). That call does
+  ggml_backend_synchronize (ggml-backend.cpp:633), so the naive "readback races the dispatch"
+  hypothesis is closed at the ggml-backend level.
